rpresser wrote:

> My first patch!  Though it's a very small one.
> 
> As has been occasionally suggested over time, this patch implements the
> ability to write your own epitaph, which will be engraved on your
> headstone and saved in the bones file. It is not displayed in the
> visual tombstone right before the game exits, nor is it saved in the
> logfile or high score list.  It only shows up on the headstone.

Well, I think I was the most recent person to mention this, so I suppose 
I should say: Thanks for posting this!

> When you die, you will be asked "Do you want to write your own
> epitaph?" right *before* DYWYPI?. If you respond with y, then you will
> be prompted with "What do you want your epitaph to be?"  Answering "I
> shouldn't have eaten the cockatrice corpse." (with the period) will be
> displayed thus when someone loads your bones file:
> 
> Something is engraved here on the headstone.--More--
> You read: "Here lies rpresser. I shouldn't have eaten the cockatrice
> corpse.".

It seems to be a slightly more flexable format without "Here lies foo." 
always at the begining might be betterm but other than that, it's 
exactly how I imagined it.

> Although the epitaph is written into the bones file, it does NOT break
> bones compatibility. The epitaph was already being written into the
> bones file as part of the grave object -- this just changes how the
> epitaph string is written.

Excelent, I figured that would be the case, but I wasn't sure.

> It gets called right before the grave is created; and as far as I can
> tell, that only happens after the system has decided to write a bones
> file. So this will tell you if a bones file was written, which is
> something that prviously you had to examine your filesystem to do
> before; and on public systems, you probably can't do that.  Should this
> be considered unbalancing then?

IMHO, no. I don't really consider that very valuable information. On a 
single player system, you can check the files anyweay, and on a multi 
player server chances are someone else will find the bones level before 
you do.

The listing your inventory thing could be a more serious problem, but 
again, at home, you can do it anyway (paper notes) and on a server 
chances are it would benifit someone else, not you. In fact, I can 
imagine people writing "And I had a wand of wishing too!" (when they 
didn't) just to mess with other players' heads more easily as listing 
all their good items. Just look at all the goofy stuff people do with 
fruit names.

Anyway if this patch catches on, it will be niteresting to see what 
people use it for.

